      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-04-17_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>Hughes —Airey.</head>
        <p>Hughes —Airey.</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON P.O. v. BOLTON P.O. • In the previous encounter on Boxing day at Bolton, Warrington were victorious by three goals to two, but on their own ground the Warringtonians could do nothing better than make a draw of it. The game was contested in a friendly spirit. The goal scored by John Gray, for W trrington was a splendid individual effort and had he had some good wing forwards to co-operate with him the Warrington team would have found their way through the coveted sticks far more frequently. A. Jones and Paulkner at back played a ,sterling game. The Bolton team played a good passing game and were rather unlucky on several occasions.</p>
      </div>
