        <p>Indigestion and Dyspepsia Can be Overcome by Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. INDIGESTION and DYSPEPSIA are mainly brought about by rich or improper foods, or the eating of food in too rapid a manner. The result is that it decomposes and fills the stomach with gas, which, pressing on the heart, makes it palpitate, or there is a disagreeable gulping of wind, or perhaps the food sours or 441r:- simply lays like a lump of nags 4 lead in the stomach. This A*-4,:,:,.4t:M produces weakness of the stomach, and before the • person is aware of it he has t;T:44IIIIEAN,' Dyspepsia fastened upon him. The proper remedy for this trouble is Dr. Morse's , Pills and c3rrect habits of eating. In all cases Dr. Nlorse's Pills should be taken 7'41 in moderate doses 'sufficient to secure a regular daily action of the bowels. All food that gives distress after eating should be avoided. Eat slowl3, and thoroughly chew • your food and take plenty of -,••t,4- - time to eat it. Mr. G. Sebopfin , . Albert Road, Southampton, -- suffered untold agony from Indigestion. He says: "I could not eat without much distress and pain. Hungry yet unable to enjoy food, suffering untold agony after each meal, it seemed as though I could stand the strain Ito longer. I was so weak that I was forced to lie ill bed. All the pleasures of life fled, and sick. miserable, and nigh unto death, gave myself up to despair. Now through Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills all is changed. Every trace of my illnesses have been removed, and to-day I am filled with vigour and health." Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills are a positive cure for Liver and Kidney Complaints, Biliousness, Indigestion, Constipation, Dyspepsia, Foul Breath, Sallow Complexion, and Female Ailments; perfect Blood Purifier, curing Eczema, Pimples and Blotches. Sold by chemists and dealers- Price IN per bottle. If unable to obtaill where you reside, The W. H. COMSTOCK Ltd.' 21 Farringdon Avenue, London, E.C., will forward same on receipt of price, post fre