        <p>Apollo Choir's Success. On Good Friday the Warrington Apollo Prize Male Choir, under the conductorship of Mr. H. Berry, obtained first prize (X 8 s. and silver-mounted baton to conductor) at the Liscard annual Eisteddfod. The test .piece was "The Crusaders." Mr. Tom Price, Merthyr, was the adjudicator, and the competing choirs were the Warrington Apollo and South Liverpool Choral Society. The adjudicator, in his remarks on the winning choir, said : "The choir possessed a fine balance of voices, the basses in par- ticular being grand, equal timbre, splendid tone, in- tonation and expression good. The prayer movement was lovely; indeed it was a grand performance." Mr. A. Greenough rendered the solo in highly credit- able style.</p>
